<item name='HFText'><text>No</text></item>
<item name='HelpECategories'><text>3. Notes System Admin Guide</text></item>
<item name='HelpESubCat'><text>New Releases</text></item>
<item name='HelpFCategories'><text>3. Guide de l'administrateur de Notes</text></item>
<item name='HelpFSubCat'><text>Nouvelle version</text></item>
<item name='HelpDocNumber'><number>3</number></item>
<item name='HelpSubCatNumber'><number>1</number></item>
<item name='HelpEHelpText'><richtext>
<pardef id='1' leftmargin='1in' tabs='L0.5000in L1in L1.5000in L2in L2.5000in L3in L3.5000in L4in'/>
<par def='1'><run><font size='12pt' style='bold underline' name='Arial' pitch='variable'
 truetype='true' familyid='20' color='red'/>2009-08-21: Note that this release has not been promoted to production yet.  It is planned to be done in August of September 2009.</run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/></run></par>
<par def='1'><run><font size='9pt' name='Arial' pitch='variable' truetype='true'
 familyid='20'/>Here is the outline of the changes that were made to all the HECS Order Tracking systems between August 2009 and September 2009.</run></par>
<pardef id='2'/>
<par def='2'><run><font style='bold underline' color='maroon'/></run></par>
<table widthtype='fixedleft' refwidth='9.1667in'><tablecolumn width='0.5000in'/><tablecolumn
 width='8.6667in'/>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<pardef id='4' keepwithnext='true' keeptogether='true'/>
<par def='4'><run><font style='bold'/>#</run></par></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<pardef id='5' keepwithnext='true' keeptogether='true'/>
<par def='5'><run><font style='bold'/>Changes</run></par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell columnspan='2'>
<pardef id='6' keepwithnext='true' keeptogether='true'/>
<par def='6'><run><font style='bold'/>Orders</run></par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'>1</par></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>Order's cost (Cost W/Applicable GST) is now applied automatically to the project's budget </run><run
><font style='underline'/>when the administrator click on the button "Got it"</run>. In the past the Administrator has to click on the button "On Order".  The button "On Order" has been removed.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>systems will detect changes of cost</run>, changes of payment method (Purchased order, MasterCard, Visa), Changes of Credit Card Holders, and changes of currency.  The amounts on the project and Credit Cards will be adjusted automatically.  The changes are detected only for the orders with the status "On Order", "Partially Received", "Received", and "Reconciled".</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'>2</par></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>button "Cancel" is now increasing the Remaining Credit on the Credit Card</run>.  The button "Cancel" cannot be used more than once. </par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'><run><font style='underline'/>Cancelled Order's cannot be modified or restored</run>.  To create a similar Order, please select the order in a view and click on the button "Copy Existing Order".</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>button "Reconciled" is now increasing the Remaining Credit on the Credit Card</run>.  Reconciled orders cannot be cancel to prevent unwanted results; the administrator can set the order's cost to zero as a work around.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>GST Exemption is now taken in consideration when updating the Remaining Credit on the Credit Cards</run>.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>button "Reconciled" is visible only if the order's status is "Received"</run>.  The partially Received orders cannot be marked as reconciled.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>"Type Mismatch" error displayed when saving some Orders has been resolved</run>.  </par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>users are now</run><run><font
 style='underline'/> forc</run><run><font style='underline'/>ed to save the new Orders before using the button "Mail to Admin"</run>.  This will prevent orders from being discarded if the validation fails and will prevent emails with broken document links to be sent to the Administrator.</par>
<par def='5'/>
