<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>GST is now taken in consideration only if the currency is Canadian "CAD"</run>.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'><run><font style='underline'/>Users with more than one first name or last name will be able to be selected in the "Send To" field on the Order Form</run>.  i.e. John Deer Smith.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>system no longer allows creation of Orders using the old form</run>.  Existing orders created for the fiscal year 2009-10 were converted to the new form.  No conversions were made on the previous fiscal years.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>button "Got It" is no longer generating new Reference Number if a number already exists</run>.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The <run><font style='underline'/>Budget and Credit Card exceeded warnings can be eliminated before the administrator click on "Got It"</run> as long as the Project's budget or the Remaining Credit on the Credit Card are modified.  The Order's cost could be lowered, the budget for the entire project could be raised, the budget for the specific category (i.e. Operating, Travel, Contract, and Capital) could be raised, or the Remaining Credit on the Credit Card could be raised.  The warnings are verified each time an orders is saved.  The warning emails are sent to the appropriate recipient only when the "Got It" button is clicked.</par>
<par def='5'/>
<par def='5'>Type of warnings: </par>
<pardef id='7' leftmargin='0.2604in' list='bullet' tabs='L1in L1.7500in L2.2500in L2.7500in L3.2500in L3.7500in L4.2500in L4.7500in L5.2500in L5.7500in'
 keepwithnext='true' keeptogether='true'/>
<par def='7'>If the <run><font style='underline'/>Monthly Limit of the Credit Card exceeds the cost of the order</run>, the application displays the warning message “WARNING!!!  You have exceeded the monthly credit card limit!!”.  If the situation is not changed when the button "Got It" is clicked, a warning email is sent to the card holder and the Section Head of the project.</par>
<par def='7'>If the <run><font style='underline'/>Order’s cost is higher than 5000$</run> the application displays the warning message “WARNING!!!  You have exceeded the $5000 per order limit!!!”.  If the situation is not changed when the button "Got It" is clicked, a warning email is sent to the card holder and the Section Head of the project.</par>
<par def='7'>If the <run><font style='underline'/>Remaining Credit amount of the Credit Card exceeds the cost of the order</run>, the application displays the warning message “WARNING!!!  The order total exceeds the available credit for this credit card.”.  If the situation is not changed when the button "Got It" is clicked, a warning email is sent to the card holder and the Section Head of the project.</par>
<par def='7'>If the <run><font style='underline'/>budget for Operation, Travel, Contract or Capital is exceeded</run>, the application displays the warning message “WARNING!!!  You have exceeded the Operating Budget Amount Limit !!!!”.  If the situation is not changed when the button "Got It" is clicked, a warning email is sent to the Principal Investigator of the project and the Section Head of the project.</par>
<par def='7'>If the <run><font style='underline'/>total budget for the project is exceeded</run>, the application displays the warning message “WARNING!!!  You have exceeded the Total Budget Limit for the project!!!”.  If the situation is not changed when the button "Got It" is clicked, a warning email is sent to the Principal Investigator of the project and the Section Head of the project.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell columnspan='2'>
<par def='6'><run><font style='bold'/>Printable Order Form</run></par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
