<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'><run><font style='underline'/>Edit History were added to most of the forms in the application</run> to track creation and modifications information.  This feature was added to facilitate the investigation if strange problems occur.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>A <run><font style='underline'/>Soft Delete feature was added to the application</run>.  The Administrator can soft delete any type of document in the application.  Soft Deleted documents are moved to the administration menu under the view "Deleted Orders".  Note that only New, Submitted and Cancelled orders can be Soft Deleted.  Soft Deleted documents can be restored by clicking on the button "Restore" located on the "Deleted Orders" view.  More details about the Soft Delete feature can be found in the Database Custodian Guide in the Help.</par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell columnspan='2'>
<par def='6'><run><font style='bold'/>Views</run></par></tablecell></tablerow>
<tablerow>
<tablecell>
<par def='4'/></tablecell>
<tablecell>
<par def='5'>The<run><font style='underline'/> icon to identify the printed orders has been modified from </run><picture
 height='18px' width='22px'><gif originalformat='notesbitmap'>
